cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hidrosentinel Nusantara (flood-map-in-rust): All-Rust Indonesian 3D Flood, GloFAS Discharge & Coastal Rob Observatory"
message: "If you use this software or methodology in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fajrianshah"
    given-names: "Evans Azka"
    affiliation: "National Research and Innovation Agency (BRIN); Graduate School, Universitas Gadjah Mada"
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
url: "https://flood.transbulent.id"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gisrad/flood-map-in-rust"
abstract: >-
  Full-stack Rust (Leptos CSR WebAssembly + Cloudflare Workers Rust + SQLite-backed Durable Objects)
  observatory monitoring 50 major Indonesian river basins and 12 coastal tidal (Rob) corridors.
  Fuses Copernicus GloFAS v4 river discharge ensembles, Open-Meteo precipitation and 2-layer soil moisture,
  Open-Meteo Marine sea-level/wave telemetry, PetaBencana.id citizen reports, BMKG CAP nowcast alerts,
  and regional flood RSS news to distinguish upstream fluvial basin surges, urban pluvial drainage inundation,
  and coastal subsidence-amplified Rob flooding, alongside deterministic AI SitRep briefings and OpenAPI/llms.txt endpoints.
keywords:
  - flood
  - indonesia
  - rust
  - webassembly
  - leptos
  - cloudflare-workers
  - durable-objects
  - glofas
  - hydrology
  - maplibre-gl
references:
  - type: article
    title: "GloFAS-ERA5 operational global river discharge reanalysis 1979–present"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Harrigan"
        given-names: "Shaun"
    journal: "Earth System Science Data"
    year: 2020
    volume: 12
    pages: "2043–2060"
